<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Albert VII, Archduke of Austria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1559–1621</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Archduke Albert</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Albert VII, Archduke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> (1559–1621), a son of Emperor Maximilian II, was a cardinal and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> of Portugal before he became governor of the Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>. In 1598 Philip II gave the provinces to his daughter Isabella Clara Eugenia, whom Albert married, and the Archdukes ruled them jointly until his death. They agreed the Twelve Years' Truce with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a> in 1609 and promoted Catholic reform and the arts in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brussels">Brussels</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antwerp">Antwerp</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/albert-vii-archduke-of-austria.jpg" alt="Albert VII, Archduke of Austria" width="320" height="445" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Workshop of Peter Paul Rubens · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rubens_-_arquiduquealbertoVII01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
